# Copy this file to .env in the server repository root, beside README.md.
# Optional settings are commented out: remove the leading # to enable a setting.
# Do not repeat a setting. Quote names/paths containing spaces or # characters.
# Native launchers read values literally, without $VARIABLE or shell expansion.
# Shell/container environment values override the same settings in this file.
#
# Preview core settings before restarting, without starting a listener or creating keys:
# Windows:     .\start-server.bat --check-config
# Linux/macOS: sh start-server.sh --check-config
# Docker:      docker compose run --rm --no-deps server python -m src.pairing --data-dir /var/lib/carriex --port 8443 --check-config
# Storage access and message TTL are also checked when the server actually starts.

# ADDRESS AND NAME
# CARRIEX_HOST: a reachable IPv4/IPv6 address or DNS hostname.
# No https://, port, path, spaces, credentials, query, or fragment.
# IPv6 may be written without brackets. Do not use wildcard 0.0.0.0 or :: here.
# Use your computer's LAN IP for phones on the same network; localhost is local only.
# DNS labels are at most 63 characters; the complete HTTPS address is at most 512.
# Do not also set the legacy CARRIEX_PUBLIC_URL: use only one address form.
CARRIEX_HOST=192.168.0.34

# CARRIEX_PORT: whole number 1-65535 inclusive; default 8443.
# This is the phone-facing port and, by default, the native/Docker host port.
# 443 works too: phones then use https://192.168.0.34 (no :443 needed).
# Native Linux/macOS may require extra privileges for ports below 1024;
# use 8443 or Docker port mapping instead of running the whole server as root.
CARRIEX_PORT=8443

# CARRIEX_SERVER_NAME: 1-80 printable characters; must not be blank.
# No newlines/control characters. Keep quotes around a name containing spaces.
CARRIEX_SERVER_NAME='Carriex-server'

# OPTIONAL STATISTICS
# Hourly measurements are saved in messages.sqlite3. Default: collection disabled.
# CARRIEX_STATISTICS: use 0 to disable or 1 to enable collection.
# CARRIEX_STATISTICS=1

# CARRIEX_STATISTICS_RETENTION_DAYS: whole number 1-365 inclusive; default 30 DAYS.
# For example, 365 is valid; 0, 1000, and fractional values are INVALID.
# An out-of-range value prevents startup, even when statistics collection is off.
# CARRIEX_STATISTICS_RETENTION_DAYS=30
# View separately on Windows: .venv/Scripts/python -m src.statistics serve
# Linux/macOS: .venv/bin/python -m src.statistics serve

# ADVANCED NATIVE SETTINGS (the standard Docker setup uses its own internal paths/port)
# CARRIEX_BIND: numeric local IPv4/IPv6 address, not a hostname or URL.
# Default 0.0.0.0 listens on all IPv4 interfaces; 127.0.0.1 allows local access only.
# CARRIEX_BIND=0.0.0.0

# CARRIEX_LISTEN_PORT: whole number 1-65535 inclusive; defaults to the port in the
# phone-facing address (CARRIEX_PORT in this example).
# Override only when a router maps the public port to a different native local port.
# Docker always listens on 8443 internally; choose its external port with CARRIEX_PORT.
# CARRIEX_LISTEN_PORT=8443

# CARRIEX_IDENTITY_DIR: writable directory; default .carriex-server.
# Use an empty/new directory or an existing Carriex identity directory, not an
# unrelated nonempty folder. Keep this directory to preserve the server's key/data.
# Native relative paths resolve from the launcher's folder. Docker uses its
# persistent server-identity volume at /var/lib/carriex instead of this setting.
# CARRIEX_IDENTITY_DIR=.carriex-server

# MESSAGE EXPIRY (native and Docker)
# CARRIEX_MESSAGE_TTL_SECONDS: positive whole number of SECONDS, not days.
# Default 2592000 = 30 days; 86400 = 1 day; 31536000 = 365 days.
# The server requires a value greater than 0. Android clients support at most
# 31536000 seconds (365 days): use 1-31536000 for Android compatibility.
# CARRIEX_MESSAGE_TTL_SECONDS=2592000

# OPTIONAL PUBLIC PAIRING EXPORT
# CARRIEX_PAIRING_EXPORT_DIR: nonblank directory path, outside the private identity
# directory. A file at this path is invalid. Exports only pairing.html/.png/.json.
# Native launchers create a missing directory; relative paths use the launcher folder.
# Docker requires an EXISTING host directory writable by the container's carriex
# user. Use an ABSOLUTE host path and add the compose.pairing-export.yaml override;
# see docs/PAIRING.md for the command.
# CARRIEX_PAIRING_EXPORT_DIR=./pairing-export

# AFTER EDITING
# Native: restart the server. Docker: apply with docker compose up -d; a plain
# docker compose restart does not load changed container environment values.
# QR/text refresh automatically; keeping the identity directory/volume preserves the key.
# More setup details: docs/PAIRING.md. Statistics details: docs/STATISTICS.md.
